0563522/week-12-seven-things-solak-thinks-chiefs-bills-giants","type":"Story","byline":"Ben Solak","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"From camcorder to Super Bowl mantra, inside Mike Macdonald's love for game film","description":"We go back to the 1980s to uncover how football bonded the 38-year-old Seahawks coach and his father.","published":"2026-11-24T11:00:21.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/50543051/seahawks-mike-macdonald-camcorder-super-bowl-game-film","type":"Story","byline":"Lindsey Thiry","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Cowboys need to break a year-long trend to make the playoffs","description":"If Dallas is going to catch up to New York in the division, it needs to start stringing wins together.","published":"2026-11-24T11:00:15.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/50573980/dallas-cowboys-nfc-east-dak-prescott","type":"Story","byline":"Todd Archer","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Jayden Daniels again delivers in 'high-pressure' situation for Commanders","description":"After failing multiple times in late-game situations earlier this season, Commanders quarterback Jayden Daniels put together a second consecutive winning drive Monday night as Washington kicked a last-second field goal to beat Cincinnati 22-20.","published":"2026-11-24T13:20:29.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/50580514/jayden-daniels-delivers-another-late-game-drive-commanders-win-vs-bengals-mnf","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"John Keim","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Commanders' Jayden Daniels-themed post aimed at Bengals tops NFL Week 11 trolls","description":"NFL teams remained petty in Week 11, led by a post from the Washington Commanders.","published":"2026-11-24T04:59:15.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/50567903/nfl-week-11-trolls","type":"Story","byline":"Anthony Gharib","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Commanders building momentum, halt Bengals' 5-game win streak","description":"The Commanders' defense held the potent Bengals in check and Washington has won three of four.","published":"2026-11-24T04:58:12.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/50573995/2026-nfl-week-11-washington-commanders-cincinnati-bengals","type":"Story","byline":"John Keim and Ben Baby","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Seahawks to monitor Sam Darnold status this week before final call vs. 49ers","description":"The Seahawks still plan to start Sam Darnold against the 49ers but will wait to see how the QB looks in practice Wednesday before making a final call.","published":"2026-11-24T02:21:45.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/50578357/seahawks-holding-final-sam-darnold-call-vs-49ers","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Brady Henderson","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"NFL Week 11 arrivals: Tee Higgins pays homage to Fiona the Hippo ahead of 'MNF'","description":"NFL stars continue to turn game-day arrivals into their own weekly fashion showcase.","published":"2026-11-24T00:12:35.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/50535179/nfl-week-11-fashionable-arrivals","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN Staff","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Struggling Ravens noncommittal on whether Humphrey will play Sunday vs. Texans","description":"A day after he was a healthy scratch in a 35-33 loss at the Panthers following a derogatory comment he made about the city of Baltimore, the Ravens were noncommittal on whether cornerback Marlon Humphrey would play Sunday against the Texans.","published":"2026-11-23T23:38:39.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/50577306/ravens-noncommittal-whether-cb-humphrey-play-sunday","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Jamison Hensley","source":"ESPN"}],"wiki":{"title":"Tay Martin","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tay_Martin","description":"American football player (born 1997)","touched":"2026-11-22T23:50:17Z","intro":"Davontavean Martin (born December 14, 1997) is an American professional football wide receiver for the Detroit Lions of the National Football League (NFL). He played college football for the Washington State Cougars and Oklahoma State Cowboys. Martin has also been a member of the San Francisco 49ers, Tennessee Titans, Washington Commanders, and the UFL's Columbus Aviators. He was signed as an undrafted free agent by the 49ers following the 2022 NFL draft.","sections":[{"key":"career","title":"Professional career","text":"SAN FRANCISCO 49ERS\nOn April 30, 2022, Martin signed with the San Francisco 49ers as an undrafted free agent. He was released during final roster cutdowns on August 30. Martin was signed to the team's practice squad the following day. He signed a reserve/future contract with the 49ers on January 31, 2023.\nOn August 29, 2023, Martin was waived by the 49ers and re-signed to the practice squad. He signed a reserve/future contract with San Francisco on February 13, 2024.\nMartin was waived by the 49ers on August 27, 2024, and re-signed to the practice squad. On September 3, Martin was released from the practice squad.\n\nTENNESSEE TITANS\nOn September 10, 2024, Martin was signed to the Tennessee Titans' practice squad. He was promoted to the active roster on January 4, 2025. In a 23-14 Week 18 loss to the Houston Texans, Martin made his first career reception on a 49-yard touchdown pass from quarterback Will Levis.\nOn May 7, 2025, Martin was waived/injured by the Titans and reverted to the injured reserve the following day. He was waived again on May 14.\n\nWASHINGTON COMMANDERS\nMartin signed with the Washington Commanders on July 23, 2025, and was released on August 26. Martin re-signed with their practice squad on September 16. He was elevated to the active roster for Weeks 4, 5, and 6, but was released from the practice squad on October 17.\n\nCOLUMBUS AVIATORS\nOn January 14, 2026, Martin was selected by the Columbus Aviators of the United Football League (UFL).\n\nDETROIT LIONS\nOn June 16, 2026, Martin signed with the Detroit Lions. For his contributions to special teams in the Week 1 win against the Saints, he received a game ball."},{"key":"personal","title":"Personal life","text":"Tay Martin is engaged to Morgan Pitre. They have two daughters, Reign and Valley."}],"wikidataId":"Q114282822","social":{}},"transactions":[{"date":"2026-07-22","text":"Waived WR Kyre Duplessis. Signed WRs Tarik Black, Lucky Jackson and Tay Martin to contracts. Placed WR Kendrick Law on injured reserve."},{"date":"2026-06-16","text":"Signed WRs Tay Martin, Tarik Black and Lucky Jackson to contracts. Placed WR Kendrick Law on injured reserve. Waived WR Kyre Duplessis."}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4245144","pfr":"https://www.pro-football-reference.com/players/M/MartTa00.htm","pff":"https://www.pff.com/nfl/players/tay-martin/61811","otc":"https://overthecap.com/player/tay-martin/10555","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tay_Martin"},"insights":["2026 cap number of $1.0M is the 44th-largest on the roster.","Contract expires after this season.","Entered the league in 2022 as an undrafted free agent."]}